+# Cricket Scorer - Professional Match Management
+
+Cricket Scorer is a high-fidelity, professional-grade Android application built with Jetpack Compose and Material 3. It is designed to provide a comprehensive match scoring and tournament management experience, inspired by top platforms like Cricinfo and Cricbuzz.
+
+## 🚀 Key Features
+
+### 1. Professional Scoring Engine
+- **Replay-Based Accuracy**: Every match is recalculated ball-by-ball from history to ensure 100% data integrity between the live score, scorecard, and player stats.
+- **Support for All Extras**: Comprehensive tracking of Wides (WD), No Balls (NB), Byes (B), and Leg Byes (LB).
+- **Match Toss Flow**: Mandatory toss and decision flow to set up the correct match roles.
+- **Dynamic Strike Rotation**: Automatic rotation based on runs and over completion.
+- **Undo Functionality**: Safe rollback of any ball while maintaining perfect player state.
+
+### 2. High-Density GUI (Cricinfo Style)
+- **Tabbed Match Center**: Clean separation between **LIVE** scoring, a full **SCORECARD**, and detailed **OVERS** history.
+- **Innings View**: Sub-tabs within the scorecard to review 1st and 2nd innings independently.
+- **Professional Bowling Tables**: High-density stats including OS (Overs), M (Maidens), R (Runs), W (Wickets), ECON (Economy), WD (Wides), and NB (No Balls).
+- **FOW (Fall of Wickets)**: Accurate records of exactly when and how each batter was dismissed.
+
+### 3. Tournament & Series Management
+- **Team Reusability**: Create teams and players once and use them across multiple matches.
+- **Leaderboards**: Automatic calculation of "Most Runs" and "Most Wickets" across the entire series.
+- **Points Table**: Dynamic standings with wins, losses, points, and simulated NRR (Net Run Rate).
+
+### 4. Device Sync & Portability
+- **.CSD Data Sharing**: Export any series to a JSON data string and import it on another device to continue scoring seamlessly.
+- **Offline First**: All data is persisted locally using GSON, meaning you can score matches without an internet connection.
+
+---
+
+## 🛠 Tech Stack
+- **Language**: Kotlin
+- **UI Framework**: Jetpack Compose (Modern, declarative UI)
+- **Design System**: Material 3 (Material Design's latest iteration)
+- **Persistence**: SharedPreferences with GSON serialization
+- **Architecture**: MVVM (ViewModel + Repository pattern)
+
+---
+
+## 📱 Installation & Requirements
+- **Minimum Android Version**: Android 7.0 (API Level 24)
+- **Target Android Version**: Android 15 (API Level 35)
+
+### How to Install:
+1. Locate the `app-debug.apk` in your project folder.
+2. Transfer the APK to your Android device.
+3. Enable "Unknown Sources" in your device settings.
+4. Open the APK and tap "Install".
+
+---
+
+## 📖 How to Use
+
+1. **Setup**: Go to the **TEAMS** tab to create your squads. Add player names to each team.
+2. **Schedule**: In the **MATCHES** tab, tap the Play button to schedule a match between two teams.
+3. **Scoring**: Tap the match card. Complete the **TOSS** to begin. Use the scoring panel to record runs, extras, and wickets.
+4. **Monitoring**: Switch to the **SCORECARD** tab at any time to see the professional match report.
+5. **Syncing**: Use the **EXPORT** button in the Series Details to share your match data with others.
+
+---
+
+## 📄 License
+This project is developed for personal use and local match management. All rights reserved.
